home='''<main id="main"><section class="hero" id="home"><div class="container hero-grid"><div class="hero-copy"><span class="eyebrow">A shared journey. A clearer future.</span><h1>Small contributions.<br>Shared possibilities.<br><span class="accent">That’s PoolPay.</span></h1><p>Bring your chit group together, keep every contribution in view, and make sense of each month’s progress. Less paperwork. More clarity.</p><div class="actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="signup.html">Start with PoolPay <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="btn btn-outline" href="how-it-works.html">See how it works <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><span class="micro">New to chit funds? Our guide is open to everyone.</span></div><div class="hero-art" role="img" aria-label="Illustrative group: 20 members contributing 5,000 rupees each form a monthly pool of 1 lakh rupees over a 20-month term."><div class="orbit"></div><span class="leaf" aria-hidden="true">✳</span><div class="pool-card"><div class="card-top">TOGETHER, EACH MONTH <span class="status">Sample group</span></div><div class="pool-value">₹1,00,000</div><p>One pool. Twenty people. Shared commitment.</p><div class="avatar-row" aria-hidden="true"><span class="avatar">AK</span><span class="avatar">SR</span><span class="avatar">NP</span><span class="avatar">RM</span><span class="avatar">+16</span></div><div class="card-rule"></div><div class="card-data"><div>Per member<br><strong>₹5,000</strong></div><div>Group term<br><strong>20 months</strong></div></div></div><div class="float-note"><strong>↗ Every contribution counts.</strong>A little consistency. A collective effort.</div><span class="art-caption">Illustrative amounts, not an available plan or offer.</span></div></div></section><div class="principles"><div class="container"><b><span>01 /</span> Built around your group</b><b><span>02 /</span> Clear contribution records</b><b><span>03 /</span> Every cycle, in one place</b></div></div>
<section class="section white" id="benefits"><div class="container"><div class="section-head"><div><span class="eyebrow">An age-old idea, made easier to follow</span><h2>Individual goals.<br>A collective way forward.</h2></div><p>A chit brings people together through regular contributions. Understanding the commitment is the first step.</p></div><div class="three-grid"><article class="feature-card"><span class="number">01</span><h3>Build a saving rhythm.</h3><p>A regular contribution gives your group a shared schedule. Choose a commitment that fits your budget for the full term.</p></article><article class="feature-card"><span class="number">02</span><h3>Understand your turn.</h3><p>Each cycle, a member receives the payout under the group’s agreement. In an auction chit, the accepted discount affects that amount.</p></article><article class="feature-card"><span class="number">03</span><h3>Keep the picture clear.</h3><p>Know what is due, what has been recorded, and how your group is progressing. Clear records help everyone stay informed.</p></article></div><a class="text-link section-link" href="how-it-works.html">Get to know the full cycle <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
<section class="section" id="features"><div class="container split"><div><span class="eyebrow">Your group, more organised</span><h2>Fewer scattered records.<br>More peace of mind.</h2><p>PoolPay gives managers and members a place to keep track of the details that matter.</p><div class="steps"><div class="step"><span>01</span><div><h3>Set up the essentials</h3><p>Managers organise groups, members, contribution amounts and schedules.</p></div></div><div class="step"><span>02</span><div><h3>Follow contributions and dues</h3><p>Record payments and review outstanding amounts without losing sight of the month.</p></div></div><div class="step"><span>03</span><div><h3>Keep a record of each cycle</h3><p>Review auction results, payout details and your group’s progress in the dashboard.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="preview"><div class="ledger"><span class="eyebrow">A clearer monthly picture</span><h3>Your group at a glance</h3><p>Example records · Month 4 of 20</p><div class="ledger-row"><span>Monthly contribution</span><strong>₹5,000</strong></div><div class="ledger-row"><span>Your payment record</span><span class="tag">Recorded ✓</span></div><div class="ledger-row"><span>Auction result</span><span class="tag">Available to review</span></div><div class="ledger-row"><span>Group schedule</span><strong>All in one place</strong></div></div><p class="preview-caption">Illustrative preview. Your dashboard reflects your group’s records.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section white" id="how"><div class="container split"><div><span class="eyebrow">Start with the basics</span><h2>One group.<br>A repeating cycle.<br><span class="accent">Everyone plays a part.</span></h2><p>Members contribute to a common pool. A payout is allocated each cycle according to the agreement, and contributions continue until the term ends.</p><a class="text-link" href="how-it-works.html">Explore our step-by-step guide ↗</a></div><div class="calculator"><span class="eyebrow">Try a simple example</span><label for="memberCount">Number of members · one ticket each</label><select id="memberCount"><option value="10">10 members</option><option value="20" selected>20 members</option><option value="25">25 members</option></select><label for="contribution">Monthly contribution per member</label><select id="contribution"><option value="2000">₹2,000</option><option value="5000" selected>₹5,000</option><option value="10000">₹10,000</option></select><span class="micro">Gross monthly pool</span><output id="poolTotal" aria-live="polite" for="memberCount contribution">₹1,00,000</output><p class="micro" id="poolTerm">20 members × ₹5,000 · 20 monthly cycles in this example.</p><p class="micro">Before any auction discount or fees. This explains the pool size; it is not a payout or return estimate.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="faq"><div class="container faq-wrap"><div class="center"><span class="eyebrow">A little clarity goes a long way</span><h2>Good questions. Clear answers.</h2></div><details><summary>Can I learn how it works without an account?</summary><p>Yes. This homepage and the complete <a class="text-link" href="how-it-works.html">How it works guide</a> are public. You only need to log in to access your account and group records.</p></details><details><summary>Is PoolPay a chit investment plan?</summary><p>PoolPay provides tools for managing chit-group records. The examples on this website are educational, not plans you can subscribe to. Check the organiser, registration and agreement of any chit you consider.</p></details><details><summary>Do I keep paying after receiving a payout?</summary><p>Yes. Receiving your payout does not end your contribution obligation. Follow the remaining payment schedule and conditions in your chit agreement.</p></details><details><summary>How do I get started as a manager or member?</summary><p>Managers can use Sign up to create an account. Members should contact their group manager for account access and group details, then use Log in to view their records.</p></details></div></section><section class="section" style="padding-top:0"><div class="container"><div class="cta"><div><h2>Your group’s next chapter,<br>a little more organised.</h2><p>Start managing with PoolPay, or learn the basics first.</p></div><a class="btn" href="signup.html">Create a manager account ↗</a></div></div></section></main>'''
Path('index.html').write_text(head('PoolPay | Together, with clarity','Understand chit funds and manage your group with PoolPay. Explore our free guide to contributions, auctions, payouts and group records.')+'<div id="landingPage">'+header()+home+footer()+'</div>\n'+Path('login-fragment.tmp').read_text(encoding='utf-8'),encoding='utf-8')
guide='''<main id="main"><section class="guide-hero"><div class="container"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="index.html">Home</a> &nbsp; / &nbsp; How it works</div><span class="eyebrow">The PoolPay guide · No login needed</span><h1>Understand the pool.<br><span class="accent">Before you take the plunge.</span></h1><p>A practical introduction to chit funds: where contributions go, how a payout is decided, and what your commitment means.</p><div class="guide-jumps"><a href="#cycle">The cycle ↓</a><a href="#terms">Key terms ↓</a><a href="#example">A worked example ↓</a><a href="#before-joining">Before you join ↓</a><a href="#faq">FAQs ↓</a></div></div></section>
<section class="section white" id="cycle"><div class="container split"><div><span class="eyebrow">01 / The idea</span><h2>Regular contributions.<br>One shared pool.</h2><p>A chit is an arrangement with a defined group, contribution schedule and term. Subscribers pay into the pool, and a subscriber becomes entitled to a payout each cycle through the method set out in the agreement.</p><p>Auctions are one common method. Other permitted methods can include a draw or tender, depending on the agreement and applicable rules.</p><div class="note">A payout is not free money. The recipient remains responsible for future subscriptions under the agreement.</div></div><div class="steps"><div class="step"><span>1</span><div><h3>Agree on the commitment</h3><p>Review the term, subscription, selection method, fees and payout conditions before joining.</p></div></div><div class="step"><span>2</span><div><h3>Contribute each cycle</h3><p>Members make the scheduled payments. Together, these form that cycle’s gross chit amount.</p></div></div><div class="step"><span>3</span><div><h3>Determine the recipient</h3><p>In an auction, eligible subscribers offer a discount they are willing to accept. Selection follows the group’s agreed auction rules.</p></div></div><div class="step"><span>4</span><div><h3>Calculate and record the payout</h3><p>The discount reduces the prize amount. Fees and the distributable share are accounted for under the agreement.</p></div></div><div class="step"><span>5</span><div><h3>Continue through the full term</h3><p>The cycle repeats for the remaining subscribers. Members who have received a payout continue their scheduled contributions.</p></div></div></div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="terms"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">02 / Know the language</span><h2>Six terms that make it click.</h2><dl class="term-grid"><div><dt>Subscription</dt><dd>The periodic contribution agreed for a ticket in the chit.</dd></div><div><dt>Gross chit amount</dt><dd>The total subscriptions for one instalment, before discount or other deductions.</dd></div><div><dt>Foreman</dt><dd>The organiser responsible for conducting the chit and administering its agreement.</dd></div><div><dt>Discount</dt><dd>The portion the selected subscriber agrees to forgo from the gross chit amount.</dd></div><div><dt>Prize amount</dt><dd>The gross chit amount less the discount; payment is subject to the agreement’s conditions.</dd></div><div><dt>Share of discount</dt><dd>The distributable portion of the discount allocated to subscribers as agreed, often called a dividend.</dd></div></dl></div></section>
<section class="section white" id="example"><div class="container split"><div><span class="eyebrow">03 / Follow the numbers</span><h2>One cycle,<br>without the guesswork.</h2><p>Imagine 20 members, each holding one ticket and contributing ₹5,000 a month, over 20 monthly cycles. The gross pool for a cycle is ₹1,00,000.</p><p>For this example, the selected member accepts a ₹20,000 discount. Assume an agreed organiser fee of ₹5,000 is taken from that discount, with the balance shared equally across all 20 tickets.</p><div class="note">The ₹750 share is an allocation of this cycle’s discount, not guaranteed interest. Whether it is paid out or adjusted against a subscription depends on the agreement.</div></div><div class="example"><span class="eyebrow" style="color:#d5e8ba">Illustration only · Not a PoolPay plan</span><h3>Where does ₹1,00,000 go?</h3><div class="ledger-row"><span>Gross monthly pool</span><strong>₹1,00,000</strong></div><div class="ledger-row"><span>Accepted discount</span><strong>₹20,000</strong></div><div class="ledger-row total"><span>Recipient’s prize</span><strong>₹80,000</strong></div><div class="ledger-row"><span>Organiser fee from discount</span><strong>₹5,000</strong></div><div class="ledger-row"><span>Remaining shareable discount</span><strong>₹15,000</strong></div><div class="ledger-row"><span>Share per ticket (₹15,000 ÷ 20)</span><strong>₹750</strong></div><p style="margin:20px 0 0">₹80,000 prize + ₹5,000 fee + ₹15,000 distributed = ₹1,00,000. Actual fees, discounts, eligibility and payout timing depend on the registered agreement.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="before-joining"><div class="container split"><div><span class="eyebrow">04 / Make an informed decision</span><h2>Clarity first.<br>Commitment second.</h2><p>Chit arrangements involve payment and organiser risks. An app or a well-presented website does not establish that a chit is registered or suitable for you.</p><ul class="checklist"><li>Verify the organiser and the chit’s registration with the relevant state authority.</li><li>Read the written agreement, including fees, default rules, exit terms and dispute procedures.</li><li>Ask about payout timing, documents, security or guarantor requirements.</li><li>Budget for every instalment, including those after your payout.</li><li>Keep receipts and reconcile your payment records with the organiser.</li></ul></div><div class="feature-card"><span class="eyebrow">Where PoolPay fits in</span><h3>The records behind<br>your group’s routine.</h3><p>Managers use PoolPay to organise groups, record contributions and maintain auction and payout details. Members use their account to follow the records made available to them.</p><p style="margin-top:18px">Recording a payment is different from transferring money. Confirm payment instructions and settlement directly with your organiser.</p><div class="actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="signup.html">Manager sign up ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="index.html?login=1">Member login</a></div></div></div></section>
<section class="section white" id="faq"><div class="container faq-wrap"><span class="eyebrow">05 / Common questions</span><h2>A few things worth knowing.</h2><details><summary>Does every member receive the same amount?</summary><p>Not necessarily. In an auction chit, the discount may vary each cycle, so prize amounts can differ. Your overall outcome also depends on fees and the shares of discount allocated over the term.</p></details><details><summary>Can I stop paying once I receive my prize?</summary><p>No. You remain liable for the remaining subscriptions under your agreement. Check any security requirements and consequences of missing a payment before participating.</p></details><details><summary>Are chit funds regulated by the RBI?</summary><p>Chit fund companies are regulated by the respective state governments, rather than by the RBI as banks. Verify a chit’s registration with the relevant Registrar of Chits. A PoolPay account does not verify or replace registration.</p></details><details><summary>Is a payout or return guaranteed?</summary><p>This guide does not promise either. Outcomes depend on the agreement, auction results, member payments and the organiser’s performance. Delays or defaults can affect participants.</p></details><details><summary>Is this example the same as my PoolPay group’s calculation?</summary><p>It may not be. This example assumes the organiser fee comes from the discount and the balance is shared across every ticket. Check your actual agreement and the calculation recorded by your manager; do not use this illustration as your payment schedule.</p></details><details><summary>Do I need an account to read this guide?</summary><p>No. You can read and share this page without logging in. An account is only needed for your private dashboard and group records.</p></details><div class="sources"><strong>Further reading</strong><p>Original educational content informed by <a href="https://kapilchits.com/#/ChitWork" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Kapil Chits</a> and <a href="https://chit.fund/how-it-works/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">chit.fund</a>. For definitions and regulation, consult the <a href="https://www.financialservices.gov.in/beta/sites/default/files/2022-10/4.%20THE%20CHIT%20FUNDS%20ACT%2C%201982.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Chit Funds Act</a> and <a href="https://rbi.org.in/scripts/PublicationsView.aspx?Id=18086" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">RBI’s financial-sector regulator overview</a>. Your agreement and applicable rules govern your chit.</p></div></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="cta"><div><h2>Understand the commitment.<br>Keep the details organised.</h2><p>Bring a clearer view to your group with PoolPay.</p></div><a class="btn" href="signup.html">Get started with PoolPay ↗</a></div></div></section></main>'''
Path('how-it-works.html').write_text(head('How Chit Funds Work | PoolPay','A free, practical guide to chit funds: contributions, auction discounts, prize amounts, member obligations and a worked example. No login required.')+header(True)+guide+footer()+'</body></html>\n',encoding='utf-8')
